Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; ============================================================================
;  Re-enable GPU Timeout Detection & Recovery (TDR)
; ============================================================================
;  WHY: this machine currently has TdrLevel = 0, which switches OFF GPU hang
;  detection entirely. When the GPU wedges, Windows never resets it and simply
;  waits — turning what should be a ~2 second recoverable driver reset into a
;  full-system hang. Evidence: 38 Event-41 hard crashes vs 1 clean shutdown in
;  14 days, with BugcheckCode 0 and no crash dump.
;
;  WHAT THIS SETS:
;    TdrLevel = 3   detect a hung GPU and recover the driver (Windows default)
;    TdrDelay = 10  wait 10 seconds before declaring a hang
;
;  Why 10 and not the 2 second default: heavy diffusion/AI kernels can
;  legitimately block the GPU for several seconds. 2s risks killing valid work;
;  10s tolerates real inference while still catching a genuine wedge.
;
;  TRADEOFF: when TDR fires it kills the running GPU job, so a long generation
;  that trips it is lost. That is strictly better than losing the whole session
;  to a hard hang.
;
;  REQUIRES A REBOOT to take effect.
;  To undo, run tdr-restore-disabled.reg (also in this folder).
; ============================================================================

[HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SYSTEM\CurrentControlSet\Control\GraphicsDrivers]
"TdrLevel"=dword:00000003
"TdrDelay"=dword:0000000a
